# The properties a mathematical object may be claimed to have: for a structure, the algebraic laws (associativity,
# commutativity, distributivity); for an order, totality and well-foundedness; for a space, completeness, compactness,
# and connectedness; for a map, injectivity, surjectivity, and continuity. A claim pairs a property with the object it
# is asserted of; the discharged ones in this library are the arithmetic and algebraic properties proved in the number,
# polynomial, and order files.
